---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro"
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Introduction"
  path="/docs/start-here/introduction"
  description="What KoAkademy is, the stack it runs on, and which path to pick."
>
  <h2>What KoAkademy is</h2>
  <p>
    KoAkademy is a <strong>self-hosted school administration and learning platform</strong>:
    a production-capable beta that ships as one deployable container. The
    repository provides a supported deployment topology and automated
    validation, while each operator remains responsible for staging, backup,
    monitoring, privacy, and recovery.
  </p>

  <h2>The stack at a glance</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Layer</th>
        <th>Technology</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Backend</td>
        <td>PHP 8.5, Laravel 12, Octane (FrankenPHP)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Administration</td>
        <td>Filament 5 with Shield permissions</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Portals</td>
        <td>Inertia 3, React 19, Tailwind CSS 4, shadcn/ui</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Data</td>
        <td>PostgreSQL; Redis for cache, sessions, and queues</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Documents</td>
        <td><code>spatie/laravel-pdf</code> with Gotenberg</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Tests</td>
        <td>Pest 4 (parallel, SQLite in-memory)</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Pick your path</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>New contributor?</strong> Start with
      <a href="/dev/development-setup">Development setup</a>, read the
      <a href="/docs/start-here/architecture">Architecture overview</a>, then dive
      into <strong>System Internals</strong>, beginning with the
      <a href="/docs/system/architecture-domain">domain model</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Maintainer?</strong> The <strong>Maintainers</strong> section
      documents the <a href="/docs/maintainers/ci">CI pipeline</a>, the
      <a href="/docs/maintainers/releases">release and versioning process</a>,
      <a href="/docs/maintainers/automation">repository automation</a>, and the
      <a href="/docs/maintainers/documentation">documentation system</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Self-hosting?</strong> Begin with
      <a href="/docs/self-hosting/installation">Installation</a>, then follow
      <a href="/docs/self-hosting/deployment">Deployment</a> and
      <a href="/docs/self-hosting/configuration">Configuration</a>. The supported
      default is one HTTPS hostname with administration at <code>/admin</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Operating a school?</strong> The
      <a href="/docs/user-guide/introduction">User Guide</a> covers daily staff
      workflows, and <a href="/docs/enrollment-policies/overview">Enrollment
      Blueprints</a> covers no-code enrollment configuration.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Integrating?</strong> Only the tested beta subset is a supported
      contract: public settings, authenticated settings, and authenticated
      student verification. See the <a href="/api/api-overview">API overview</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="doc-callout doc-callout-caution">
    <p class="doc-callout-label">Supported versions</p>
    <p>
      Only the latest stable release is supported. KoAkademy is licensed under
      <strong>GNU AGPL-3.0-or-later</strong>.
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
